WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:04.471
Speaker 1: All right, Mississippi is in real
trouble when it comes to the pandemic, and

00:00:04.471 --> 00:00:05.620
they are not messing around.

00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:11.790
They are now threatening five years in prison
for people who skip covid isolation if it

00:00:11.790 --> 00:00:14.840
involves a life threatening situation.

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:17.710
So let's take a look at what is going on here.

00:00:17.710 --> 00:00:24.289
Covid-19 patients must isolate or face fines
under the new Mississippi Department of Health

00:00:24.289 --> 00:00:30.140
order as covid-19 cases across the state continue
to surge.

00:00:30.140 --> 00:00:34.390
State health leaders are hoping a new order
will encourage people infected to self isolate.

00:00:34.390 --> 00:00:38.870
Friday, state health officer Dr. Thomas Dobbs
handed down a mandate that all individuals,

00:00:38.870 --> 00:00:44.630
vaccinated or not, who test positive must
stay home upon learning they are infected.

00:00:44.630 --> 00:00:45.960
This is the key part.

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:49.890
Individuals who fail to do so could be charged
with a misdemeanor punishable by a fine of

00:00:49.890 --> 00:00:54.470
five hundred dollars, six months imprisonment
or both upon conviction.

00:00:54.470 --> 00:00:57.380
And then here's the key key line.

00:00:57.380 --> 00:01:02.380
If a life threatening disease is involved,
failure to follow the order could result in

00:01:02.380 --> 00:01:10.000
a failed felony charge, carrying a fine of
up to five thousand dollars five years in

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:12.310
prison or both.

00:01:12.310 --> 00:01:17.630
The news comes as Mississippi continues to
report thousands of new infections daily and

00:01:17.630 --> 00:01:22.240
as it leads the nation in new cases per 100000
inhabitants.

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:24.880
There are people saying this is crazy, this
is too much.

00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:29.570
But understand what is happening in Mississippi,
Mississippi at baseline.

00:01:29.570 --> 00:01:35.100
This is pre covid and during it, just aside
from covid, Mississippi is fiftieth out of

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:38.480
50 in health care rankings in the United States.

00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:40.820
This includes access, cost and quality.

00:01:40.820 --> 00:01:46.600
OK, Mississippi is also the second least vaccinated
state in the country.

00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:51.280
There are ahead of only Alabama and even then
only by half a point.

00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:54.040
Basically, Mississippi and Alabama are together.

00:01:54.040 --> 00:02:00.940
The two least vaccinated states in the country,
Mississippi, is out of ICU beds.

